            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Morrie Shepard Killian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great recipe! The only changes I made were I rendered the salt pork first and added it back with 2 cups of my own chicken stock. My family all like their collards different, some like sweet, some like spicy, I just like a little butter, so I let them make those adjustments at the table. 10 minutes before serving, I sprinkle some extra diced ham into the pot. I serve over grits with hush puppies on the side. It is a favorite meal at my house.",
